{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I was [A]born in the Southland, twenty some odd years ago
Now I [A]ran away for the first time when I was about four years old
I'm a free born [D]man, my home is on my [A]back
Lord, I [E]know every inch of highway and
every foot of back road and
every mile of a railroad [A]track
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I got a gal in Cincinnati, got a woman in San Antoine
But I always love that girl next door and any ole place is home
I'm a free born man, my home is on my back
Lord, I know every inch of highway and
every foot of back road and
every mile of a railroad track
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I've got me a worn out guitar, I carry an ole tote sack
I've hocked it about two-hundred times but I always get it back
I'm a free born man, my home is on my back
Lord, I know every inch of highway and
every foot of back road and
every mile of a railroad track
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
You may not like my appearance, you may not like my song
You might not like the way I am but you sure like the way I'm gone
I'm a free born man, my home is on my back
Lord, I know every inch of highway and
every foot of back road and
every mile of a railroad track
{end_of_verse}
